    "detailed_description": "House of Moir\u00e9 presents a <strong>marriage of op-art and immersion.</strong> In this linear, non-game and atmospheric piece, the visitor <strong>advances through rooms of an otherworldly home</strong>, choosing where to pause, look and listen as the <strong>surrounding architecture</strong> and <strong>sound objects </strong>reveal themselves. <br><br><strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">FEATURES</h2></strong><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Transforming optical patterns <br></li><li> 6DOF<br></li><li>Audio-visual programming <br></li><li>Minimalist spatial design <br></li><li>Live processed field recordings </li></ul><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2100760/extras/8e652fe800967f83de8283a8f41ef47d.poster.avif?t=1689288288\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2100760/extras/8e652fe800967f83de8283a8f41ef47d.webm?t=1689288288\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2100760/extras/8e652fe800967f83de8283a8f41ef47d.mp4?t=1689288288\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div><br><strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">TREATING SPACE AS AN INSTRUMENT</h2></strong>House of Moir\u00e9 is the culmination of various iterations of Moir\u00e9, a series of A/V works that explore <strong>fascinations with psycho-acoustics, sound spatialization, sensory illusion, and real-time virtual environments.</strong> Experimental and surreal, House of Moir\u00e9 invites a <strong>temporary escape into an alternative space.</strong> It is made with<strong> custom audio software, depth cameras, motion capture, and interactive design principles.</strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\"><strong>ABOUT THE ARTISTS</strong></h2><strong>Chloe Alexandra Thompson</strong> and <strong>Matthew Edwards </strong>(aka aesthetic.stalemate) are interdisciplinary artists and collaborators. Chloe is a composer and sound designer interested in the physicality of sound and mediation of technology in installation and performance, and Matthew blends installation art, performance and virtual reality.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">PART OF MUTEK'S <strong><i>IMMERSIVE COLLECTION</i></strong></h2>An electronic music and digital arts festival for 23 years, now navigating the artistic possibilities of VR.<br><br><strong>MUTEK acknowledges the support of the Canada Council for the Arts.</strong>",
    "about_the_game": "House of Moir\u00e9 presents a <strong>marriage of op-art and immersion.</strong> In this linear, non-game and atmospheric piece, the visitor <strong>advances through rooms of an otherworldly home</strong>, choosing where to pause, look and listen as the <strong>surrounding architecture</strong> and <strong>sound objects </strong>reveal themselves. <br><br><strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">FEATURES</h2></strong><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Transforming optical patterns <br></li><li> 6DOF<br></li><li>Audio-visual programming <br></li><li>Minimalist spatial design <br></li><li>Live processed field recordings </li></ul><div class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2100760/extras/8e652fe800967f83de8283a8f41ef47d.poster.avif?t=1689288288\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2100760/extras/8e652fe800967f83de8283a8f41ef47d.webm?t=1689288288\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2100760/extras/8e652fe800967f83de8283a8f41ef47d.mp4?t=1689288288\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div><br><strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">TREATING SPACE AS AN INSTRUMENT</h2></strong>House of Moir\u00e9 is the culmination of various iterations of Moir\u00e9, a series of A/V works that explore <strong>fascinations with psycho-acoustics, sound spatialization, sensory illusion, and real-time virtual environments.</strong> Experimental and surreal, House of Moir\u00e9 invites a <strong>temporary escape into an alternative space.</strong> It is made with<strong> custom audio software, depth cameras, motion capture, and interactive design principles.</strong><h2 class=\"bb_tag\"><strong>ABOUT THE ARTISTS</strong></h2><strong>Chloe Alexandra Thompson</strong> and <strong>Matthew Edwards </strong>(aka aesthetic.stalemate) are interdisciplinary artists and collaborators. Chloe is a composer and sound designer interested in the physicality of sound and mediation of technology in installation and performance, and Matthew blends installation art, performance and virtual reality.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">PART OF MUTEK'S <strong><i>IMMERSIVE COLLECTION</i></strong></h2>An electronic music and digital arts festival for 23 years, now navigating the artistic possibilities of VR.<br><br><strong>MUTEK acknowledges the support of the Canada Council for the Arts.</strong>",
    "short_description": "An audio-visual artwork. Enter a void-like shapeshifting realm and visit a succession of rooms dressed in optical patterns, responsive audio programming, and minimalist spatial design. Adapted from a live show by Chloe Alexandra Thompson &amp; Matthew Edwards.",
